cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ember or its cleaned data, please cite it as below, and cite the NASA PSI datasets by their DOIs."
title: "Ember: will a small fire keep burning in habitat air? Learning from NASA microgravity combustion experiments"
authors:
  - name: "Ember Team (NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026)"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hassanbil999/Ember"
url: "https://mohamad-755--freefall-atlas-web.us-east.modal.run"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Ember cleans 19 NASA Physical Sciences Informatics combustion tables (1,848 tests) and, from the two that record
  whether a flame survived, trains models validated on test campaigns they never saw, giving an estimate only near
  real tests. In NASA's gas-jet tests no flame stayed lit below 30 % oxygen, and none were run between 25 % and 33 %,
  the oxygen range planned for a Moon base.
keywords:
  - microgravity combustion
  - spacecraft fire safety
  - NASA Space Apps
  - Gaussian process
  - open data
